A worker has 7 days in a week and can choose one of two strategies to maximize the total amount of work completed.

Strategy 1: Work x units every day for all 7 days.

Strategy 2: Work y units per day for the first d days, then work z units per day for the remaining 7 - d days.

Given the values of d, x, y, and z, determine the maximum amount of work the worker can complete in one week.

Input Format
A single line contains four space-separated integers : d x y z

Output Format
Print a single integer representing the maximum amount of work that can be completed in one week.




#include <iostream>
#include <bits/stdc++.h>
using namespace std;
int main()
{
    int d,x,y,z;
    cin>>d>>x>>y>>z;
    int n=7;
    int st1=x*7;
    int st2=d*y + (7-d)*z;
    if(st1>st2){
        cout<<st1;
    }
    else{
        cout<<st1;
    }
    return 0;
}
